IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ccc-core`
IMPORT `ccc2-sedition`

-- ccc2-tests-sedition.l4 -- tests for ccc2-sedition.l4 (ss 59 to 62). Expected values are written beside each assertion from the text of the provision,
-- before the run. The s 787(1) penalty is a seam input: the tests pass a placeholder that states nothing.

§ `Tests -- section 59(4), the presumption (lines 1029-1033)`

--                                                                  teaches advocates writing  force  without authority  governmental change
#ASSERT `s 59(4) the person is presumed to have a seditious intention` TRUE  FALSE TRUE  TRUE  TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- (a) teaches or advocates
#ASSERT `s 59(4) the person is presumed to have a seditious intention` FALSE TRUE  TRUE  TRUE  TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- (b) publishes or circulates a writing that advocates
#ASSERT `s 59(4) the person is presumed to have a seditious intention` TRUE  FALSE FALSE TRUE  TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- not the use of force
#ASSERT `s 59(4) the person is presumed to have a seditious intention` TRUE  FALSE TRUE  FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- with the authority of law
#ASSERT `s 59(4) the person is presumed to have a seditious intention` TRUE  FALSE TRUE  TRUE  FALSE EQUALS NOTHING  -- not as a means of accomplishing a governmental change
#ASSERT `s 59(4) the person is presumed to have a seditious intention` FALSE FALSE TRUE  TRUE  TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- neither teaches nor publishes: "Without limiting the generality" leaves the term open

§ `Tests -- section 60, the exception (lines 1034-1042)`

--                                                         intention                                                                                                            good faith  by reason only
#ASSERT `s 60 the person is deemed to have a seditious intention` `s 60(a) to show that Her Majesty has been misled or mistaken in her measures` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 60 the person is deemed to have a seditious intention` `s 60(b)(i) to point out errors or defects in the government or constitution of Canada or a province` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 60 the person is deemed to have a seditious intention` `s 60(b)(ii) to point out errors or defects in Parliament or the legislature of a province` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 60 the person is deemed to have a seditious intention` `s 60(b)(iii) to point out errors or defects in the administration of justice in Canada` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 60 the person is deemed to have a seditious intention` `s 60(c) to procure, by lawful means, the alteration of any matter of government in Canada` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 60 the person is deemed to have a seditious intention` `s 60(d) to point out, for the purpose of removal, matters that produce or tend to produce feelings of hostility and ill-will between different classes of persons in Canada` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 60 the person is deemed to have a seditious intention` `s 60(a) to show that Her Majesty has been misled or mistaken in her measures` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- not in good faith
#ASSERT `s 60 the person is deemed to have a seditious intention` `s 60(a) to show that Her Majesty has been misled or mistaken in her measures` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- not "by reason only" of that intention
#ASSERT `s 60 the person is deemed to have a seditious intention` `s 60 another intention` TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- the two together: (4) read with 60.
--                                                    teaches advocates writing force  w/o auth gov.  intention                                                                                good faith by reason only
#ASSERT `s 59(4) and s 60 the person has a seditious intention` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE `s 60(c) to procure, by lawful means, the alteration of any matter of government in Canada` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- "Notwithstanding subsection 59(4)"
#ASSERT `s 59(4) and s 60 the person has a seditious intention` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE `s 60 another intention` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 59(4) and s 60 the person has a seditious intention` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE `s 60(a) to show that Her Majesty has been misled or mistaken in her measures` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- good faith, but the presumption does not rest only on that intention
#ASSERT `s 59(4) and s 60 the person has a seditious intention` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `s 60(a) to show that Her Majesty has been misled or mistaken in her measures` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Tests -- section 59(1) to (3), seditious words, libel and conspiracy (lines 1023-1028)`

#ASSERT `s 59(1) the words are seditious words` (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 59(1) the words are seditious words` (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 59(1) the words are seditious words` NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 59(2) the libel is a seditious libel` TRUE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 59(2) the libel is a seditious libel` FALSE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- not a libel
#ASSERT `s 59(2) the libel is a seditious libel` TRUE (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 59(2) the libel is a seditious libel` TRUE NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 59(2) the libel is a seditious libel` FALSE NOTHING EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- "an agreement between two or more persons": two is enough, one is not.
#ASSERT `s 59(3) the agreement is a seditious conspiracy` 2 (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 59(3) the agreement is a seditious conspiracy` 3 (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 59(3) the agreement is a seditious conspiracy` 1 (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 59(3) the agreement is a seditious conspiracy` 0 (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 59(3) the agreement is a seditious conspiracy` 2 (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 59(3) the agreement is a seditious conspiracy` 2 NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Tests -- section 61, punishment of seditious offences (lines 1043-1048)`

--                                                          act                                       words answer  libel answer  conspiracy answer
#ASSERT `s 61 the person commits a seditious offence` `s 61(a) speaks seditious words` (JUST TRUE) NOTHING NOTHING EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 61 the person commits a seditious offence` `s 61(b) publishes a seditious libel` NOTHING (JUST TRUE) NOTHING EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 61 the person commits a seditious offence` `s 61(c) is a party to a seditious conspiracy` NOTHING NOTHING (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 61 the person commits a seditious offence` `s 61(a) speaks seditious words` (JUST FALSE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- the words are not seditious words
#ASSERT `s 61 the person commits a seditious offence` `s 61(a) speaks seditious words` NOTHING (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 61 the person commits a seditious offence` `s 61 an act that is none of those in paragraphs (a) to (c)` (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 61 the class of the offence` EQUALS `an indictable offence`
#ASSERT `s 61 the punishment` EQUALS LIST Punishment OF `by indictment`, `imprisonment for a term of` `fourteen years`, `no imprisonment is stated`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`

§ `Tests -- section 62, offences in relation to military forces (lines 1049-1057)`

--                                                    Canadian Forces answer  foreign forces member  lawfully present
#ASSERT `s 62(2) the person is a member of a force` (JUST TRUE) FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- (a) the Canadian Forces
#ASSERT `s 62(2) the person is a member of a force` (JUST FALSE) TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- (b) forces of another state lawfully present in Canada
#ASSERT `s 62(2) the person is a member of a force` (JUST FALSE) TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- not lawfully present: "means"
#ASSERT `s 62(2) the person is a member of a force` (JUST FALSE) FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 62(2) the person is a member of a force` NOTHING FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- s 2 "Canadian Forces" leaves it open
#ASSERT `s 62(2) the person is a member of a force` NOTHING TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 62(2) the person is a member of a force` NOTHING TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
--                                                               act                                                                                                                   intentionally  member of a force answer
#ASSERT `s 62(1) the person commits an offence in relation to a member of a force` `s 62(1)(a) interferes with, impairs or influences the loyalty or discipline of a member of a force` TRUE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 62(1) the person commits an offence in relation to a member of a force` `s 62(1)(b) publishes, edits, issues, circulates or distributes a writing that advises, counsels or urges insubordination, disloyalty, mutiny or refusal of duty by a member of a force` TRUE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 62(1) the person commits an offence in relation to a member of a force` `s 62(1)(c) advises, counsels, urges or in any manner causes insubordination, disloyalty, mutiny or refusal of duty by a member of a force` TRUE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 62(1) the person commits an offence in relation to a member of a force` `s 62(1)(a) interferes with, impairs or influences the loyalty or discipline of a member of a force` FALSE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING   -- not intentionally
#ASSERT `s 62(1) the person commits an offence in relation to a member of a force` `s 62(1)(a) interferes with, impairs or influences the loyalty or discipline of a member of a force` TRUE (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- not a member of a force
#ASSERT `s 62(1) the person commits an offence in relation to a member of a force` `s 62(1)(a) interferes with, impairs or influences the loyalty or discipline of a member of a force` TRUE NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 62(1) the person commits an offence in relation to a member of a force` `s 62(1) an act that is none of those in paragraphs (a) to (c)` TRUE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 62(1) the class of the offence` EQUALS `an offence that the section makes both indictable and punishable on summary conviction`
#ASSERT `s 62(1) the punishment` (Punishment OF `on summary conviction`, `no imprisonment is stated`, `no imprisonment is stated`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`) EQUALS LIST (Punishment OF `by indictment`, `imprisonment for a term of` `five years`, `no imprisonment is stated`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`), (Punishment OF `on summary conviction`, `no imprisonment is stated`, `no imprisonment is stated`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`)
